  "body": "## What\n\nFirst real test batch for the ~101-script untested gap flagged by\n`PLATFORM_COMPLETION_CHECKLIST.md` (generated by\n`generate_platform_completion_checklist.py` against the live DB).\nReal dispatch UMR-20260806-175915-8f47, steps 4-7 (steps 1-3, the status\ncorrection, were handled by the sibling in-flight task\nUMR-20260806-175649-66e4 / a676b792dc65a5437 -- not duplicated here).\nGoverning authority: Owner absolute stop-work order\ntask-20260806-165921-owner-absolute-stop-work-order--complete.\n\nReal baseline confirmed by running the generator fresh (not a stale\ncommitted copy): **47/148** scripts genuinely complete+tested.\n\nCross-referenced the real 101-script untested list against scripts this\nsession's dispatch/governance/reporting path repeatedly touches. Two of the\nexplicitly-named load-bearing scripts (`dispatch_core.py`,\n`resource_governor.py`, `dispatch-tick.py`, `superboss-register.py`,\n`generate_pm_report_v3.py`) turned out to ALREADY be genuinely tested --\nverified against the real checklist rather than assumed. The two that were\ngenuinely untested (`gtm_write_category_result.py`,\n`worker-entrypoint.sh`), plus 6 more genuinely load-bearing untested\nscripts on the same dispatch/supervision/governance paths, got real,\npassing tests in this batch:\n\n- `gtm_write_category_result.py` -- canonical GTM certification-category\n  result writer every `gtm_check_*.py` script calls.\n- `worker-entrypoint.sh` / `doc-worker-entrypoint.sh` -- the two systemd\n  worker entrypoints; tests extract the real lifetime-invocation-cap block\n  and the real PREFLIGHT-GUARD-BLOCK (both scripts' own header comments\n  already said \"tests/preflight_guard_hardstop_test.sh extracts this\" --\n  that file was never actually written until now) verbatim from the live\n  file and run them in an isolated harness with `python3`/`systemctl`\n  intercepted via PATH stubs.\n- `resource_governor_tick_loop.sh` -- real `run_governor()` exit-2\n  (argparse usage error) escalation-to-ATTENTION.md path.\n- `supervisor-sweep.sh` -- real end-to-end run against a fixture task dir\n  via the script's own already-documented `VERIDIAN_TASKS_DIR`/\n  `VERIDIAN_SWEEP_LOG_DIR` override seam.\n- `owner_status.py` -- real isolated-DB test of the reconciled task-status\n  table + `--verify-live` mismatch detection.\n- `recover-failed-workers.py` -- real 402-balance-failure signature\n  matching + dry-run safety.\n- `metadata_reconciliation.py` -- real path-token extraction/resolution\n  logic + isolated-DB `knowledge_engine` read helpers.\n\nReal new count immediately after this batch (before rebase): **55/148**.\nAfter rebasing onto the latest `origin/main` (which merged 2 unrelated,\nalready-tested scripts + their own tests in the interim -- confirmed via\ndiff, not assumed), the real total is now **150** real scripts, **57**\ngenuinely complete+tested. Real remaining untested count: **93** scripts.\nThis is explicitly a first batch, not full closure -- the order's\n\"148/148 (now 150/150) or documented exceptions\" call is left for a future\ncycle per this dispatch's own scope.\n\n## Real evidence\n\n- `python3 generate_platform_completion_checklist.py` output before batch:\n  `{\"scripts\": \"47/148\", \"tables\": \"35/42\", \"search\": \"10/10\"}`\n- Same command after batch: see committed `PLATFORM_COMPLETION_CHECKLIST.md`\n  / `.json`.\n- Every new test file genuinely passes under `pytest -q`, run individually\n  and as part of the full suite via the checklist generator's own\n  `_run_pytest()`.\n\n## Hard limits respected\n\nNo OCID-020/Z.AI/external-agent work resumed. PR #169/#196 not merged. No\ncredential rotation. No repository deletion/archival. Worked in an isolated\nworktree/clone, never directly in `/opt/veridian/scripts`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
